Organ sync feature — reactive + periodic reconciliation

Every mutation to a synced entity (record, record extension, concept, assertion, etc.) passes through one central change-handling function. That function already fans out to whatever features are enabled for the record (e.g. broadcasting the update over WebSocket via Protein to subscribed SAND components in real time). Sync should be added as another optional feature on that same path, not a separate pipeline.

Two complementary mechanisms:

1. Reactive delta sync — on every write to a synced table, immediately push the small delta to each organ this node is synced with. Cheap, instant, keeps organs converged in near-real-time.
2. Periodic hash reconciliation — every 5 minutes, hash each synced table per organ pairing and compare hashes with the remote organ instead of transmitting full data. Diff efficiently to find divergence, then reconcile only the differing records. This is the safety net that catches anything the reactive path missed (dropped messages, races, etc.), without the cost of full-copy transfers or full-merge computation each cycle.

